<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12165" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cynŏcĕphălus</span></b> ,
			i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυνοκέφαλος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An ape with a dog's head</i> (in Africa): Simia
			inuus, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 30, 35, § 190</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 54, 80, §
			216</span></i>; <i><span class="en">37, 9, 40,
				§ 124</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 6, 1,
			25</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The dog-headed Anubis</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Tert. Apol.
			6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A kind of wild man</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 11, 3, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12,
				2, 32</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
